==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|hlaibaz|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|kel-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{proto|ine-pro|kley-|title=|lang=ang}}.  Cognate with Old High German {{term|hleib|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Laib|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|hleifr|lang=non}} (Old Swedish ''lēver''), Gothic {{term|𐌷𐌻𐌰𐌹𐍆𐍃|tr=hlaifs|lang=got}}.  The Indo-European root is also the source of Ancient Greek {{term|κλίβανος||baking oven|tr=klibanos|lang=grc}}, Proto-Slavic {{recons|xlěbъ|lang=sla-pro}} (Russian {{term|хлеб||bread|lang=ru}}, Polish {{term|chleb||bread|lang=pl}}).

